+## Science/estimate-flavoured data viz
+Requested `create-stack`: a stacked chart of "amount of life in the universe"
+from the Big Bang to heat death, explicitly asking for the metric to be
+defined (quantity × quality of experience) and for it to be an "estimate" —
+another instance of the mechanism-over-magic preference (see above), this
+time applied to a speculative/order-of-magnitude domain rather than a clean
+formula. Built with real cited order-of-magnitude figures where they exist
+(population estimates, standard extinction dates) and clearly flagged
+speculation where they don't, rather than presenting invented future numbers
+with the same confidence as sourced ones — worth keeping as the default for
+any future "estimate X" request: show the real number where one exists, mark
+the guess where it doesn't, don't blend the two. Rainbow chrome + plain dark
+reading surface applied again without being asked, consistent with the
+established default. No direct feedback yet since this is a first turn.
